  "title": "Priority-0 pre-answer material exact-match clamp and score-time chronology guard",
  "non_claim": "This is not clean external replay success, compact-gate confirmation, deletion authority, benchmark authority, or a review court.",
  "risk_addressed": "The current lane could spend a distinct custodian on a response that the final scorer later rejected for blank answers, null attestations, bad cost accounting, or hand-entered timing. It also duplicated strict JSON/hash/time/output primitives across stage tools, increasing drift and fail-late risk.",
  "repair_summary": "A responder-visible init/finalize helper now captures observed hashes and stage times, validates every required answer and per-packet/total cost before custody, requires explicit clean-preanswer attestation, writes a new immutable candidate, and refuses overwrite. One scorer-free shared response contract is rerun by responder finalization, custody intake, score-sheet preparation, and final scoring. Shared strict-artifact primitives now centralize duplicate-key/non-finite rejection, timezone parsing, hashing, and write-new behavior across all three kits. Stage times are helper-captured rather than operator CLI arguments, while remaining explicitly non-trusted local-clock evidence.",
